One important thing about 100% branch coverage

There is a difference between fixing your tests and actually covering this production branch:

.bodyValue(requestBody == null ? Mono.empty() : requestBody)

Your current implementation's null branch is actually broken.

This:

.bodyValue(Mono.empty())

doesn't mean "send an empty body." It means "send a Reactor Publisher as the body object," which bodyValue() doesn't allow.

If you want 100% branch coverage including the requestBody == null branch, I recommend fixing the production code rather than avoiding the branch in tests.

Change:

.bodyValue(requestBody == null ? Mono.empty() : requestBody)

to:

.body(
    requestBody == null
        ? org.springframework.web.reactive.function.BodyInserters.empty()
        : org.springframework.web.reactive.function.BodyInserters.fromValue(requestBody))

Or add the import:

import org.springframework.web.reactive.function.BodyInserters;

and use:

.body(
    requestBody == null
        ? BodyInserters.empty()
        : BodyInserters.fromValue(requestBody))

Then you can have a proper test for the null branch:

@Test
@DisplayName("sendFlexRequest - successful request with null body")
void sendFlexRequest_success_withNullBody() throws Exception {

    server.enqueue(
        new MockResponse()
            .setResponseCode(200)
            .setHeader(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_TYPE, "application/json")
            .setBody("{}"));

    JsonNode result =
        subject
            .sendFlexRequest(
                "test-endpoint",
                HttpMethod.GET,
                Collections.emptyMap(),
                null,
                JsonNode.class)
            .block();

    assertNotNull(result);

    RecordedRequest request =
        server.takeRequest(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

    assertNotNull(request);
}

I strongly recommend this production change

Because otherwise you're effectively saying:

> "I want 100% coverage, but I don't want to execute the null branch because executing it exposes a real bug."



The better solution is to fix the null-body handling and then test it.


